== TES Common Applications (0.8.1)

.Release Information
[width="30%"]
|====================================
| Date              | 2019-08-16
| Release Label/Tag | 0.8.1
| AIS Template		| 4.0
| Released By       | Subba Gundala
|====================================

== Release Summary Information

=== us803653 - CPM 2.0 SA: TMAC/Telemetry data to Telematics using SFT (machas3)

Added PCS/Loader Cycle TMAC/Telemetry data to FileTransferBridgeApp.

=== us792913 - Improve/Simplify DataLinkData  (machas3)

Refactored DataLinkParam and DataLinkParamInfo to move all "static" metadata to 
DataLinkParamInfo and variable data to DataLinkParam.  Made the following 
client-side changes:

	- DataLinkData::GetParams - Allows iteration through the internal container 
	  using C++11 range-based for loops.  Usage (const is optional):
        for (const DataLinkParam& dlParam : dataLinkData.GetParams())
            {
                switch (dlParam.GetParamId())
                    { ...
	- DataLinkData::AddDataLinkParam - Now returns false if all necessary metadata 
	  for the parameter has not been set.
	- DataLinkData::UpdateDataLinkParam - Now returns false if the update failed.
	- DataLinkData::GetParamByID - New function that provides a pointer to the 
	  DataLinkParam with the provided PID and ParameterIdType.  Overloads are 
	  provided if the Parameter comes from another source (i.e. SID/Source Address
	  and DataLinkType)
	- DataLinkData::GetParamValueIndexByName, GetParamValueIndexByPID - Deleted, 
	  they were poorty implemented functions that returned 0 ( a valid index) if
	  the parameter was not found.
	- DataLinkParam::SetLastValue - Can take either a vector<unsigned_8> or 
	  uint32_t for fixed length PIDs.  In either case, lastValue should be the raw,
	  unpacked value read from the datalink.  DSI is required, i.e. lastValue 
	  cannot be set without the DSI and vice versa.
	- DataLinkParam::SetLastValueDsi – Removed per changes to SetLastValue
	- DataLinkParam::SetVarLengthParamValue - Sets the lastValue for variable 
	  length PIDs.  Can take either a vector or uint8_t array.
	- DataLinkParam::SetLastValueEng - New function that allows the engineering 
	  value to be directly set for fixed length PIDs.  Raw value is computed 
	  based on Scaling and Offset and stored internally.  Simplifies internal 
	  publish of DataLinkData.
	- DataLinkParamInfo::GetDataLinkTypeString, GetParamIdTypeString, 
	  GetParameterTypeString, GetUnitsString, VarLengthDataLinkParamFactory::
	  GetVarLengthParamTypeString - New functions to get std::string representations
	  for the corresponding data.  Used for OCS plugin that will eventually appear 
	  in eta-ais, can also be used for debugging.

===  us808416 - Fix unsupported JSON parser special characters and symbols (machas3)

Updated Bmi Autogen to replace . and \ characters in JSON keys with spaces.

=== us783857 - AU2020 L2: Configure weighing app to use datalink inputs (machas3)

Extended PwmInputChannels to allow direct access to the PWM Inputs.

===  us805716 - Make preferred J1939 address configurable through ruby (divyaa)

Supported for configuring the J1939 Preferred address through j1939 ruby file instead of 
configuring through application.

=== us807412 - Review log statements in BmiJ1939 (divyaa)

Removed unnecessary logs from J1939 and changed logging to appropriate log level.

=== us807762 - Support parameter types in one J1939 JSON config (divyaa)

Support PIDs and PGNs in one JSON config file. Each parameter type has separate tag for 
PID’s, PGN’s and CAT EXT ID’s. Application needs to look for key 
BMI_J1939_CONFIG_JSON_FILE_PATH in ruby file instead of 2 or 3 JSON file paths such as 
BMI_J1939_PGN_CONFIG_JSON_FILE_PATH and BMI_J1939_CDL_PID_CONFIG_JSON_FILE_PATH in 
machine specific robot file. Update Automation scripts as well for combined PID and
PGN in one J1939 config JSON file. J1939 App would exit with proper error messages 
if JSON parsing fails and as well if required PROP-A PGN is not added under PGN 
section in JSON config file.

=== us800941 Verify PGN, MAP, CAT EXT ID with Variable length (divyaa)

Updated BmiJ1939 to support variable length params such PGN’s, PID’s through MAP and CAT Ext ID’s.

=== us804666 Add support for CAT Ext Ids in BmiEthernet app (gundas1)

Added support for CAT Ext ids in BmiEthernet app. Found a CSNS bug that's not 
passing data status in the handler. So, BmiEthernet app doesn't communicate
data status properly. We will have fix in next release 0.10.0 assuming
CSNS would have fix by then.

